              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you're hauling temperature-sensitive cargo, choosing the right reefer trailer isn't just important; it's mission-critical. Whether you're transporting frozen foods, pharmaceuticals, or anything in between, the right refrigerated trailer helps ensure your products stay protected, your customers stay satisfied, and your operation runs smoothly.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "But with so many models, configurations, and features available, how do you know you're making the right call? Here's what to look for when buying new reefer trailers, so you can invest confidently in the equipment that keeps your business moving.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-why-new",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Why Investing in a New Reefer Trailer Pays Off",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "why-new"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-why-new-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Buying new may require more upfront, but for businesses that rely on consistency, compliance, and fuel efficiency, the long-term value is worth it.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-why-new-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Latest Compliance Standards",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Avoid fines and meet federal and state regulations."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Better Fuel Efficiency",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Newer models are built to reduce emissions and save on operating costs."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Improved Insulation",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Modern reefer trailers have better thermal control and temperature retention."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Lower Maintenance",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "New equipment means fewer breakdowns and warranty-backed peace of mind."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-factors",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Factors That Impact Reefer Trailer Selection",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "factors"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-factors-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Every business is different. When you're narrowing down reefer trailers for sale, make sure the specs match your cargo needs, driving patterns, and long-term goals.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-factors-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Type of Cargo",
                        "points": [
                          {
                            "text": "Frozen foods require lower, more stable temperature ranges"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Produce and floral goods need ventilation and humidity control"
                          },
                          {
                            "text": "Pharmaceuticals demand high-tech temperature logging and secure insulation"
                          }
                        ]
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Distance and Route Conditions",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Long hauls require better insulation, larger fuel tanks, and dependable reefer units. Regional routes may benefit from lighter trailers with faster cycling refrigeration systems."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-factors-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "<strong>Refrigeration unit type:</strong>",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "list-factors-4",
                  "type": "prose-list",
                  "props": {
                    "ordered": false,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Diesel-powered units are common and offer strong cooling capacity"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Electric standby can reduce idling costs during loading and unloading"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Hybrid models offer flexibility and lower fuel consumption"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-features",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Features to Look for in a New Reefer Trailer",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "features"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-features-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The difference between a good trailer and the right trailer often comes down to smart features that align with your business goals.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "cards-features-2",
                  "type": "card-lists",
                  "props": {
                    "variant": "type",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "title": "Advanced Insulation",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Look for high value materials and seamless wall design."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Air Chute Systems",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Ensure consistent airflow to all areas of the trailer."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Telematics and Temperature Monitoring",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Critical for compliance and customer reporting."
                      },
                      {
                        "title": "Swing or Roll-Up Doors",
                        "points": [],
                        "intro": "Choose based on your loading dock setup and route needs."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "actions-features-3",
                  "type": "buttons",
                  "props": {
                    "align": "left",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "ctaId": "browse-trailers",
                        "label": "Check Out Our Inventory",
                        "style": "primary"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-mistakes",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Common Mistakes to Avoid",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "mistakes"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-mistakes-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Even experienced buyers can overlook key details. Avoid these missteps to protect your investment and avoid costly downtime.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-mistakes-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "mark": "dot",
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Ignoring maintenance requirements — some models require more frequent service than others; know your maintenance plan before you commit"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Overlooking weight and payload balancing — a lightweight trailer may save on fuel but could compromise durability; always verify your payload needs and legal load limits"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Assuming one size fits all — what worked for your last trailer might not be ideal for your current routes or cargo"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Forgetting about resale value — high-quality reefer trailers hold their value better; look for models with strong brand reputations and robust warranty support"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-faq",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "FAQs About Buying New Reefer Trailers",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "faq"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "questions-faq-1",
                  "type": "qa-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "q": "What size reefer trailer do I need?",
                        "a": "Most standard reefers are 53 feet, but shorter options are available. Your choice depends on what you're hauling and where you're going."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "How often should a reefer unit be serviced?",
                        "a": "Follow the manufacturer's maintenance schedule. Typically, expect service every 750 hours of operation or every 3-6 months."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "What brands should I consider?",
                        "a": "Look for trailers from brands known for durability, compliance, and service support. Sun State Trailers partners with proven manufacturers like Hyundai Translead."
                      },
                      {
                        "q": "Should I finance or lease?",
                        "a": "If you plan on long-term use, buying provides better value. Leasing may be ideal for seasonal hauls or short-term contracts."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-faq-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "When cargo quality and compliance are on the line, your trailer choice matters. Buying new gives you the advantage of updated technology, fewer maintenance issues, and long-term reliability. At <a href=\"/locations/trailer-sales\">Sun State Trailers</a>, we understand that Florida businesses depend on efficient, hard-working trailers that won't let them down.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-faq-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "We carry reefer trailers for every kind of hauler, from food service to pharmaceuticals. Let us help you find the one that fits.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
